A||||11||Ken Wittlief||2.8L how do you remove the distributor||||1||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-18-2001||11:20 PM||||I took my chiltons manual back to the library yesterday, I want to pull the dist so I can get at the cold start injector and see if its leaking.<P>  I pulled the 15mm bolt out and marked the body position, and i took the half moon shaped plate off.<P> the dist spins loosely - as it does when setting the timing, but it only lifts up about a 32nd of an inch from the block.<P>  whats holding it in? is there another screw somewhere? does the engine have to be at TDC to pull the dist?! what gives?<P>  I've pulled on it pretty hard while twisting it - feels like a snap ring or something is holding it in still.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||05-18-2001||11:28 PM||||I replaced my distributor last fall and had the same problem. There is no snap ring that I remember, its just a very snug fit for about one to one and a half inches. Of course the dist should turn a little as the distributor's worm gear comes off of the cam's worm gear. <P>When I installed the replacement distributor it was also a very snug fit as it went down. I personally used the handle part of a ball pin hammer to coax the new dist down. Its slow work but you should be able to get the old one out and the new one back in.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-18-2001||11:41 PM||||Good firm upwards jerk and it'll pop out. careful not to catch it in the forehead.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>there is nothing else but the 15 m bolt with horseshoe clip.  try to put a new o ring on dist or use pipe dope with old if you don't have a new ring.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-19-2001||12:07 AM||||come on - you guys gotta be yanking my chain and sitting there laughing at me.<P> the dist is completely loose and the shaft the rotor sits on moves up and down about an 8th of an inch easily<P> and I can only pull it up about a 32nd of an inch - it doenst bind, it still twists freely, and the shaft still moves up and down<P>  so it the body is loose and the shaft is loose then whats holding it in?!?!?!?<P>  I stood in the trunk with one foot onthe intake manifold, that puppy is dead solid, like its held in with a something. Even when Im pulling up on it hard it still turns freely.<P>  this just doesnt make any sense. how can it turn so easily, but not pull out?||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||05-19-2001||12:11 AM||||When I did mine at work I thought the same thing.  Called over a more experienced guy and said whats up with this and he pushes it down into place and with a firm pull up it pops out, leav'in me look'in dumb.<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 05-19-2001).]||||reg||1
