Z||000008||EdsB52||05-19-2001||08:45 PM||||When I changed mine it was frozen solid. I had to destroy the mother-focker to get it out. I took a crescent wrench just under the base-plate and turned it back-and-forth barely. It took all I had to do that. Then I used something (I forget what) to pry up on the distributor base and after about two hours of focking with it, it finally came out trashed! I bought a new one and guess what? It wouldn't fit. I had to take sandpaper to the round body that slips into the intake and sand a few thousandth off until it fit. I'm guessing maybe a lip exists at the base of your distributor underneath the intake.||||reg||1
Z||000009||beer_stud_21||05-19-2001||09:12 PM||||nope ken, that really is how it comes out.  I had to pull mine a while ago to replace the pickup coil.  I had a bit of trouble getting mine out also, but mine would come about an inch of the way out then stop.  I finally "twist and pull"  till it came out.  maybe try putting some kind of penetrating oil all the way around to see if you can get it to come out easier.   Good luck, and whatever you do resist the urge to use the BFH.. hehe<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||05-20-2001||01:18 AM||||Just to let you know - I never did get the dist out - found the cause of my engine problems - was something else - see thread: "creature damage"||||reg||1
